  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 21—Miscellaneous",
    "Division 1—Applications and other documents",
    "21.2  Requirements for filing documents"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "21.2",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r21.2",
  "text": "(1) A document that is required to be in an approved form and that is filed must be in English and be legible. (2) If any other document is filed: (a) the document must be in English, be in the form (if any) specified in a direction under section 213B of the Act and be legible; or (b) the following apply: (i) the document (the original document) must be filed with a document (the translated document) that is a translation of the original document into English; (ii) the original document must be filed with a certificate of verification; (iii) the translated document must be in the form (if any) specified in a direction under section 213B of the Act and be legible. (3) Subregulation (2) does not apply in relation to an application mentioned in paragraph 4.11(1)(a), 5.18(2)(a) or 17A.19(1)(a). Note: Regulations 4.11, 5.18 and 17A.19 have specific rules about applications filed in trade marks offices (however described) of Convention countries.",
  "title": "Requirements for filing documents",
